   "conversationId": "2102817072887550247",
   "text": "In addition to site-neutral payments, decreasing governmental regulation, and increasing payment to private practice physicians.  Lets see this:\nTax incentives- allow  private practice physicians to qualify for the FULL QBI tax deduction, just like a trade.  Medicine is classified as a specified service trade.  If we want more independent doctors, we have to make independence economically viable. We give tax incentives to businesses because we want those businesses to exist. Why wouldn't we do the same thing for independent medical practices? The beneficiary isn't just the doctor. The beneficiary is the patient who gets another choice .  We want to make it easier for small private practices to thrive. @SecScottBessent @WaysandMeansGOP @DrOzCMS",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-23T17:47:13.000Z",
