   "url": "https://x.com/STzorfas/status/2097737457122882010",
   "conversationId": "2097737457122882010",
   "text": "I am involved in almost all aspects of my practice.  Something I noticed for a long time depositing secondary-insurance checks.  Checks labeled Aetna, HealthSpring, United American, ACE Property & Casualty, Aflac, American Retirement, Loyal American Life all appear to be drawn on the same UMB Bank account and have the same routing information.  All have check numbers beginning with the same series, ie. 136…., 137……..\n\nDoes anyone in insurance/payment processing know why multiple apparently unrelated insurers would issue claims payments from the same bank account/payment system? Is this simply a centralized payment processor, or is there a corporate relationship I’m missing?  I still like to do everything on paper and I do whatever I can to get paper checks. Is this why they don’t want anybody getting paper checks?\n\n@AAPSonline @AARP @AMACforAmerica",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-09T17:22:38.000Z",
