   "conversationId": "2088266736239870334",
   "text": "SITE-NEUTRAL MEDICARE PAYMENTS.  LETS BRING THE RECEIPTS!\n\nA study by Brady Post, PhD, Edward C. Norton, PhD, and colleagues found that Medicare paid 80% more for the same outpatient services when billed by a hospital outpatient facility rather than an independent physician.\n\nIn 2010, the same bundle of services was worth $141,000 per physician PER YEAR when billed from an independent physician’s office—but $240,000 per physician PER YEAR when billed through a hospital outpatient facility.\n\nThat's a $99,000 PER PHYSICIAN, PER YEAR difference for the same services.\n\nAt the time, site-neutral payment was estimated to save Medicare about $11 billion over 10 years.\n\nBut that estimate is now outdated. In 2024, the Congressional Budget Office estimated that broader site-neutral payments could save Medicare approximately $157 BILLION over 10 years.\n\nA 2025 Health Affairs study from Johns Hopkins examined several Medicare site-neutral payment proposals. Depending upon how broadly site-neutral payment was applied, the estimated reduction in Medicare payments to hospitals ranged from $212 million to $7.36 billion annually.\n\nThis isn't just about saving taxpayers money. Medicare's payment system creates a powerful financial incentive for hospitals to acquire independent physician practices.\n\nWe need site-neutral payments—and a private-practice physician on the Medicare advisory committee.\n\nThe people actually practicing independently need a voice at the table.\n\nSave taxpayers money. Preserve physician autonomy. Preserve private practice.\n@DrOz #saveprivatepractice @NeilFlochMD @DrDiGiorgio",
