   "id": "2080630503518994519",
   "url": "https://x.com/STzorfas/status/2080630503518994519",
   "conversationId": "2080630503518994519",
   "text": "I just tried to fill a 3-month prescription for generic Alrex eye drops.\n\nNo matter where I look—using my insurance or paying cash—the cost is about $720 for a 3-month supply. Sometimes it's even over $1,000.\n\nAt the same time, Medicare continues proposing cuts to physician reimbursement that threaten independent private practices.\n\nPatients are paying more. Independent physicians are being paid less. Yet healthcare costs keep rising.\n\nWe know the real drivers of rising healthcare costs aren't independent physicians—they're the ever-increasing costs associated with hospitals, insurers, and prescription drugs. Independent doctors shouldn't be the ones continually asked to absorb more cuts.\n\nIt's time to give practicing independent private physicians a seat at the table when Medicare policy is developed. The physicians who care for patients every day deserve a voice in the decisions that affect patient access to care.  \n#SavePrivatePractice #DrugPrices @CMSGov @DrOz",
   "lang": "en",
